      "worked_solution": "Recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for sine with $u=x$ and $v=\\frac{5\\pi }{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-\\frac{5\\pi }{3}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
